  "answer_text": "Despite his name, Flounder from *The Little Mermaid* is **not actually a flounder**. \n\nBecause he is a fictional cartoon character, his species varies depending on which version of the movie you are watching:\n\n### 1. In the 1989 Animated Film: A Tropical Angelfish / \"Guppy\"\n* **The Inspiration:** In the original animated classic, Flounder is a vibrant, chubby, yellow-and-blue tropical fish. While he is a stylized cartoon creation rather than a perfect representation of one specific fish, animators heavily modeled his colorful design and round body after a **tropical reef fish, most likely a saltwater angelfish** (such as a blue or royal angelfish).\n* **The \"Guppy\" Label:** In the movie, Ariel's father, King Triton, and other characters mockingly refer to him as a \"guppy\" (leading to his famous line, *\"I'm not a guppy!\"*). *The Little Mermaid* animated prequel TV series later leans into this joke, officially classifying him as a guppy (his school records list him as \"Guppy Number 35\"), even though he looks nothing like a real-life tiny guppy.\n\n### 2. In the 2023 Live-Action Remake: A Sergeant Major\n* **The CGI Version:** For the photorealistic 2023 live-action movie, Disney based Flounder\u2019s design on a real-world fish. He is officially depicted as a **Sergeant Major** (*Abudefduf saxatilis*), which is a species of **damselfish**. Like animated Flounder, real-life Sergeant Major fish have bright yellow upper bodies and vertical blueish-black stripes, though the CGI adaptation sparked plenty of internet memes for looking a bit drabber and \"skinnier\" than the chubby 1989 cartoon.\n\n### What is a *real* flounder?\nA real-life flounder is a type of **flatfish** that lives camouflaged on the muddy ocean floor. They are flat, diamond-shaped, dull brown or speckled grey in color, and as they mature, both of their eyes migrate to one side of their head so they can look upward while lying flat on the sand. Real flounders look nothing like the cute, round, bright yellow-and-blue Disney sidekick!",
